<title>USA: Biomune's Adair retires as president.</title>
<headline>Biomune's Adair retires as president.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biomune Systems Inc said Monday Milton Adair, has retired as president. He will remain a director and become a consultant to the company, it said.</p>
<p>David Derrick, chief executive officer, will assume the position of president, it said. Derrick will continue as CEO and as chairman, it added.</p>
<p>Derrick said Biomune will focus on sales of its &quot;nutraceutical&quot; products and the research and development of its drugs designed to help the immune system combat disease.</p>
</text>
